{# Both halves of the courses list: the courses the viewer is on, then
   everything else. Rendered standalone (htmx, from `get_fragment_courses`, on
   every keystroke in the filter box) and inlined by `index-logged-in.jinja` on
   first paint, so the filtered list and the initial one cannot drift apart.

   Context: `courses` (`{enrolled, non_enrolled}` from `query_courses`), `q`,
   the filter as it was typed - the empty states say different things depending
   on whether one is in force - and `is_admin`, which is not read here but is
   inherited by the cards. #}

<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
  <div>
    <h2 class="font-bold text-lg">Your courses</h2>
    <p class="text-[13px] text-base-content/55">
      The ones you are enrolled on, whether as staff or as a student.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
  {% for course in courses.enrolled %}
  {% include "_course-card.jinja" %}
  {% else %}
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-base-300 bg-base-200/40 px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-base-content/50">
    {% if q %}
    None of your courses match “{{ q }}”.
    {% else %}
    You are not enrolled on any course yet.
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mt-8 mb-3">
  <div>
    <h2 class="font-bold text-lg">Other courses</h2>
    <p class="text-[13px] text-base-content/55">
      Everything else on this server. Enroll to join one as a student.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
  {% for course in courses.non_enrolled %}
  {% include "_course-card.jinja" %}
  {% else %}
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-base-300 bg-base-200/40 px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-base-content/50">
    {% if q %}
    No other course matches “{{ q }}”.
    {% else %}
    There are no other courses.
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
